int termination = 10;

In Java, we can encapsulate the provided problem statement in a class 'OddNumberCalculator'. It will consist of two instance fields 'commencement' and 'termination' to specify the range. It will also consist of three methods:

- 'findOddNumbers()' to find the odd numbers in the given range.
- 'calculateAverage()' to calculate the average of these numbers.
- 'checkForException()' to handle potential exceptions and errors.

Here is an optimized and clean code as per the problem requirements:

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class OddNumberCalculator {
    private int commencement;
    private int termination;
    private ArrayList<Integer> oddNumbers;

    public OddNumberCalculator(int commencement, int termination) throws IllegalArgumentException {
        if (commencement > termination) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid range input. Start point is greater than end point.");
        }
        this.commencement = commencement;
        this.termination = termination;
        this.oddNumbers = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    public ArrayList<Integer> findOddNumbers() {
        for (int i = this.commencement; i <= this.termination; i++) {
            if (i % 2 != 0) {
                this.oddNumbers.add(i);
            }
        }
        if (this.oddNumbers.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("No odd numbers in the specified range.");
        }
        return this.oddNumbers;
    }

    public double calculateAverage() {
        if (this.oddNumbers.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("No odd numbers calculated yet.");
        }
        double sum = 0;
        for (int i : this.oddNumbers) {
            sum += i;
        }
        return sum / this.oddNumbers.size();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            OddNumberCalculator calculator = new OddNumberCalculator(1, 10);
            System.out.println("Odd numbers: " + calculator.findOddNumbers());
            System.out.println("Average: " + calculator.calculateAverage());
        } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
            System.out.println("Error occurred: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
